{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And he set it up as a pillar.</b> He did not set up a pillar in the place where he slept, which is Beersheba, but in Bethel, which is Jerusalem, and it is the place opposite which the top of the ladder reached." "<b>And he poured oil upon its top.</b> The pouring of oil, or the libation of wine, upon a pillar is like the offering of a sacrifice upon the altar. <b>And Rabbenu</b> Saadiah Gaon, of blessed memory, wrote that the pouring of the oil here was for recognition, so that he would recognize the stone and distinguish it in his mind from all others, for the impression of oil upon a stone is visible — thus far his words." "<b>And they said in the Midrash:</b> When Jacob returned to gather the stones, he found them all to be one stone, and he set it up as a pillar in the midst of the place, and oil came down for him from heaven, and he poured oil upon it, as it says: ״ויצק שמן על ראשה״. What did the Holy One, blessed be He, do? He took His right foot and pressed this stone down into the depths of the abyss, and made it a support for the earth, like a man who makes a support for a dome; therefore it is called אבן שתיה (the Foundation Stone), for He set it as the navel of the earth, and from there the earth was spread out, and upon it the temple of HaShem stands, as it says: ״והאבן הזאת אשר שמתי מצבה יהיה בית אלהים״. And from there he lifted his feet and went to Haran in the blink of an eye."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:15:56.749741564Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}